{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the quota of the bricks.</b> The fixed tally of the bricks that each one would produce per day when straw was given to them — that same quota you shall impose upon them now as well, so that the labor be heavy upon them." "<b>For they are idle.</b> From labor — therefore their hearts turn to idleness, and they cry out saying, <b>Let us go, etc.</b>" "<b>The quota.</b> And וְתֹכֶן לְבֵנִים — ״וְלוֹ נִתְכְּנוּ עֲלִילוֹת״ (1 Samuel 2), ״אֶת הַכֶּסֶף הַמְתֻכָּן״ (2 Kings 12) — all are terms of reckoning." "<b>Idle.</b> The work is slack in their hands and abandoned by them, and they are slack toward it; רטריי״ט בְּלַעַ״ז."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {2 "Rashi writes only ותכן לבנים (without quotation marks or introductory formula); it appears to be a second biblical occurrence of the root, cited as parallel evidence.", 3 "the la'az is Old French retreit/retrait, 'withdrawn/slack'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:40.460578936Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}